Integration approach — what each upstream contributed:

 • Directory name: Adopted flow 0's agent_foundation/ui/widgets/ (matches
   existing widget_protocol.py noun, pairs with Dash) but recorded flow 1's
   react/ alternative as OQ-15 with full trade-off captured.
 • Package name: @agent-foundation/ui-widgets (flow 0).
 • Phase structure: Adopted flow 1's cleaner 7-phase decomposition (Phase 0
   bootstrap, Phase 6 cleanup) wrapped around flow 0's richer per-phase
   content (more granular acceptance criteria, risks, validation, rollback for
   Phases 1–5).
 • Widget-contract direction: Adopted flow 1's clearer source-of-truth flow
   (Python widget_protocol.py → widget_schema.py emits JSON Schema → TS
   codegen), unified with flow 0's transport-agnostic, version-aware
   WidgetRegistry design and adapt() migration hook.
 • Theme contract: Took the union — flow 0's cssVariableBridge (key for Dash
   interop) + zIndex tokens + chat-specific colors, plus flow 1's
   ThemeProvider wrap + clear MUI/emotion cache ownership story.
 • Packaging: Reconciled to MUI 5 floor with ^5 || ^7 peer range + CI matrix
   on both majors; workspace consumption Phases 0–4 → internal npm publish in
   Phase 5 → 1.0 in Phase 6.
 • Risk register: Merged 11 (flow 0) + 10 (flow 1) into 16 deduped,
   severity-rated entries (5 🔴 / 7 🟡 / 4 🟢).
 • Open questions: Merged into 17 OQs covering MUI baseline, distribution
   form, vendored-webui deprecation, Dash validation adoption,
   single-vs-split, TS-vs-JS, transport metadata, Storybook hosting,
   visual-regression tool, codemod ownership, dual builds, versioning, naming,
   CSS-only build, directory-name widgets/ vs react/, token governance,
   IP/licensing.
 • Timeline: Added flow 1's explicit ≈ 7.5-week timeline table.
 • Validation strategy: Combined flow 0's bench/contract JSON-artifact
   discipline with flow 1's per-phase rollback drill and contract-fixture
   count target (≥ 20).

The integration consistently keeps dash_interactive/ untouched, webui/
frozen-then-deprecated, and widget_protocol.py extended (additive,
backward-compatible). All concept snippets remain illustrative — no
implementation code reproduced.

Integration judgment: The two upstream artifacts overlapped on the core thesis
(single React library, peer-dep React 18+MUI 5, phased migration,
Python-as-truth for widget contract) but diverged on several non-trivial
design points — directory name, phase count, source-of-truth direction for
codegen, cssVariableBridge for Dash, distribution timeline, and unique
risks/OQs in each. The integration surfaced genuinely new signal: a cleaner
combined phase plan, a more complete risk register, a unified set of open
questions, and a reconciled directory/naming decision that captures both
perspectives.

