## Original User Request
**Description**: Design the target architecture for shared UI in agent_foundation/ui and author the staged migration plan. Using the catalog (subtask 1) and canonical contracts (subtask 2), decide: (a) destination layout — propose creating agent_foundation/ui/widgets/ (or agent_foundation/ui/react/) with sub-namespaces {primitives, chat, chat-widgets, layout, theme, hooks} and clarify how it coexists with the existing agent_foundation/ui/webui (which appears to be a vendored copy of rankevolve) and the Python dash_interactive surface; (b) packaging — single internal React library, peer-deps strategy (peer-dep React 18 + MUI 5 baseline so rankevolve and agent_foundation/webui can consume; openteam upgrades down to that baseline OR we publish dual builds); (c) theme contract — minimal token schema that the shared theme module exposes; (d) widget contract — unified Python widget_protocol ↔ React WidgetRegistry alignment; (e) phased migration plan with explicit phases (Phase 1: primitives + theme + hooks; Phase 2: chat primitives; Phase 3: chat-widgets + WidgetRegistry; Phase 4: layout; Phase 5: consumer adoption in openteam, rankevolve, and agent_foundation/webui) including per-phase risks, rollback strategy, and open questions requiring user decision (e.g., React/MUI baseline, monorepo vs. pip-installable JS package).

**Todos**:
- Define the destination directory layout under agent_foundation/ui and justify it against existing dash_interactive + webui surfaces
- Decide and justify the React/MUI/emotion peer-dependency baseline
- Specify the theme token contract (color, spacing, radii, typography) and how createAppTheme/themeRegistry/ThemeSwitcher generalize
- Specify the unified Widget contract reconciling React WidgetRegistry/ChatWidgetRenderer with agent_foundation/ui/widget_protocol.py
- Author phased migration plan with per-phase scope, deliverables, risks, validation steps, and rollback
- Author consumer adoption guide for openteam, rankevolve, and agent_foundation/webui (imports to change, version bumps, theme wiring)
- Enumerate open questions/decisions for user sign-off (e.g., MUI 5 vs MUI 7 baseline, whether to deprecate the vendored webui copy in AgentFoundation)
</OriginalUserRequest>

