  Contract (Decision D)\n 207 \n 208 Shared schema name: WidgetSpec. Python is  
  the source of truth (widget_protocol.py); a generator emits JSON Schema; TS   
  bindings are generated from the JSON Schema.\n 209 \n 210 text\n 211          
  WidgetSpec = {\n 212   id:          string                # stable client     
  id\n 213   kind:        string                # discriminator: "approval" |   
  "choice" | "confirmation" |\n 214                                      #      
  "multiple_choice" | "single_choice" | "text_input" |\n 215                    
  #   "conversation_tool" | "markdown" | "image" |\n 216                        
  #   "table" | "plot" | <custom>\n 217   version:     int                   #  
  integer major; minor changes are additive (OQ-12)\n 218   title?:             
  string\n 219   description?:string\n 220   payload:     Record<string, any>   
  # widget-kind-specific (schema-validated)\n 221   actions?:    Array<{ id;    
  label; style?; payload?: any }>\n 222   state?:      "pending" | "submitted"  
  | "expired" | "error"\n 223   created_at:  string                #            
  ISO-8601\n 224   metadata?:   Record<string, any>   # tracing, agent ids,     
  timestamps\n 225 }\n 226 \n 227 WidgetAction = {\n 228   widgetId:            
  string\n 229   actionId:    string\n 230   values?:     Record<string, any>   
  # form-style returns from input widgets\n 231   timestamp:   string           
  # ISO-8601\n 232 }\n 233 \n 234 \n 235 #### Python side (source of truth)\n   
  236 - widget_protocol.py (extended, backward-compatible):\n 237   -           
  Discriminated-union envelopes on kind using pydantic.BaseModel.\n 238   -     
  Adds version: int, id: str, created_at: datetime, metadata: dict[str,         
  Any].\n 239   - class WidgetProtocol(BaseModel) plus subclasses               
  (MarkdownWidget, ImageWidget, TableWidget, ChoiceWidget, FormWidget,          
  PlotWidget, ApprovalWidget, ConfirmationWidget, MultipleChoiceWidget,         
  SingleChoiceWidget, TextInputWidget, ConversationToolWidget,                  
  CustomWidget).\n 240   - Methods: to_spec() -> WidgetSpec,                    
  from_action(action: WidgetAction), serialize_for_react() returns a            
  JSON-serializable envelope consumable over any transport (websocket, SSE,     
  postMessage from a Dash iframe).\n 241   - Exposes WIDGET_SCHEMA (the JSON    
  Schema produced by pydantic).\n 242 - widget_schema.py (new):\n 243           
  python\n 244   def emit_schema(path: pathlib.Path) -> None: ...\n 245   #     
  Invoked via Makefile target / pre-commit hook; writes\n 246   #               
  agent_foundation/ui/widgets/schemas/widget-spec.schema.json\n 247   \n 248    
  \n 249 #### TypeScript side\n 250 - scripts/generate-protocol.ts runs         
  json-schema-to-typescript against widget-spec.schema.json → emits             
  src/protocol/widget.generated.ts (header: // GENERATED — do not edit).\n 251  
  - chat-widgets/WidgetRegistry.ts:\n 252   ts\n 253   type WidgetKind =        
  WidgetSpec[\'kind\'];\n 254   interface WidgetRenderer<K extends WidgetKind>  
  {\n 255     kind: K; version: number;\n 256     component:                    
  React.ComponentType<{ spec: Extract<WidgetSpec, {kind: K}>; onAction: (a:     
  WidgetAction) => void; }>;\n 257   }\n 258   class WidgetRegistry {           
  register(...); get(kind, version); render(spec, onAction);                    
  adapt(fromVersion, toVersion) }\n 259   \n 260   The registry is              
  transport-agnostic and version-aware (per-widget version + adapt() migration  
  hook for forward-compat).\n 261 - chat-widgets/ChatWidgetRenderer.tsx: thin   
  component <ChatWidgetRenderer spec={spec} registry={registry}                 
  onAction={onAction} />. Validates spec against JSON Schema in dev-mode only   
  (opt-out in prod). Provides <UnknownWidgetFallback /> when version/kind       
  lookup fails, with a telemetry event.\n 262 \n 263 #### CI drift check\n 264  
  scripts/check-protocol-drift.sh:\n 265 1. Re-emits widget-spec.schema.json    
  from Python (python -m agent_foundation.ui.widget_schema).\n 266 2. Re-runs   
  generate-protocol.ts.\n 267 3. git diff --exit-code on the generated          
  files.\n 268 \n 269 Wired into pre-commit + CI.\n 270 \n 271 Why              
  headless+typed: this is the only design that satisfies both surfaces (Dash    
  sends JSON; React consumes JSON) without coupling either to the other's       
  framework.\n 272 \n 273 ---\n 274 \n 275 ## 3. Phased Migration Plan\n 276    
  \n 277 Each phase has: scope, deliverables, acceptance criteria, risks,       
  validation, rollback. Phases are sequential; within a phase, sub-items can    
  parallelize. "Done" = acceptance criteria all green + at least one consumer   
  integration test green where applicable.\n 278 \n 279 ### Phase 0 —           
  Bootstrap (≈ 2–3 days, no consumer changes)\n 280 Scope: scaffold             
  agent_foundation/ui/widgets/ (package.json, tsconfig, tsup, vitest, lint, CI  
  matrix on MUI 5 & 7, Storybook). Add webui/README.md DEPRECATED notice.       
  Inventory out-of-tree consumers of vendored webui (R-07).\n 281 \n 282        
  Deliverables: empty package builds & publishes a 0.0.0 smoke artifact; CI     
  green; Storybook hosting decided (OQ-8).\n 283 \n 284 Risks: 🟢 Tooling       
  churn.\n 285 \n 286 Validation: pnpm -F @agent-foundation/ui-widgets build    
  && pnpm -F @agent-foundation/ui-widgets test && npm pack succeed in CI.\n     
  287 \n 288 Rollback: delete widgets/ directory; no consumer touched.\n 289    
  \n 290 ### Phase 1 — Theme + Primitives + Hooks (Foundation, ≈ 1 week)\n 291  
  Scope: port primitives (LoadingIndicator, EmptyState, SectionCard,            
  StatusBadge, PersonChip, ProgressBar, QuickLinkButton, PendingReasonPopover,  
  MarkdownRenderer, Button, Card, Stack, Icon, Tooltip), theme/*, generic       
  hooks/* from rankevolve & openteam, reconciling APIs to the token schema.\n   
  292 \n 293 Deliverables\n 294 - widgets/src/{primitives,theme,hooks}/* with   
  Storybook stories per export.\n 295 -                                         
  widgets/src/theme/{tokens,createAppTheme,themeRegistry,ThemeProvider,ThemeSw  
  itcher,cssVariableBridge,legacy}/*.\n 296 - CI: lint + typecheck + unit       
  tests + storybook build.\n 297 \n 298 Acceptance criteria\n 299 - pnpm -F     
  @agent-foundation/ui-widgets build produces ESM + CJS + .d.ts.\n 300 - A      
  scratch app on React 18 + MUI 5 renders every primitive without errors.\n     
  301 - A scratch app on React 19 + MUI 7 renders every primitive without       
  errors.\n 302 - createAppTheme(lightTokens) survives both MUI v5 and v7 type  
  checks.\n 303 - Theme tokens snapshot test passes; 100% of exports have       
  Storybook story + TSDoc.\n 304 \n 305 Risks\n 306 - 🟡 MarkdownRenderer has   
  three subtly-different versions across codebases. Mitigation: pick            
  rankevolve's (smallest deps) as canonical, file diffs as backlog.\n 307 - 🟡  
  Subtle MUI v5↔v7 API drift inside primitives. Mitigation: CI matrix against   
  both; encapsulate MUI calls inside primitives.\n 308 - 🟢 Bundle size growth  
  — mitigated by sub-path exports + size-limit (<25 kB gz for primitives).\n    
  309 \n 310 Validation: jest/vitest + RTL unit tests; visual regression        
  baseline via @storybook/test-runner; type-coverage ≥ 95%.\n 311 \n 312        
  Rollback: package unimported by any consumer; rollback = delete widgets/      
  directory.\n 313 \n 314 ### Phase 2 — Chat Primitives (≈ 1 week)\n 315        
  Scope: promote chat-leaf components, headless w.r.t. transport (no fetch, no  
  websocket).\n 316 \n 317 Deliverables: widgets/src/chat/* — MessageList,      
