  widgets/bench/results.json (not stdout).\n 332 \n 333 Rollback: revert        
  sub-path; consumers still on local copies; widgets/src/chat/* can stay        
  (unused).\n 334 \n 335 ### Phase 3 — Chat-Widgets + WidgetRegistry (the       
  contract phase, ≈ 1.5 weeks)\n 336 Scope: deliver the unified WidgetSpec      
  schema, Python ↔ React alignment, and all chat-widget renderers.\n 337 \n     
  338 Deliverables\n 339 - widgets/schemas/widget-spec.schema.json (single      
  source).\n 340 - widgets/src/protocol/widget.generated.ts (generated TS       
  types).\n 341 - agent_foundation/ui/widget_protocol.py extended (additive);   
  new agent_foundation/ui/widget_schema.py emitter.\n 342 -                     
  widgets/src/chat-widgets/builtins/{Approval,Choice,Confirmation,MultipleChoi  
  ce,SingleChoice,TextInput,ConversationTool,Markdown,Image,Table,Plot}Widget.  
  tsx.\n 343 - widgets/src/chat-widgets/{WidgetRegistry.ts,                     
  ChatWidgetRenderer.tsx, legacy/}.\n 344 - End-to-end fixture: Python harness  
  emits a WidgetSpec, React harness renders it, user "submits", React emits a   
  WidgetAction, Python deserializes and validates it.\n 345 \n 346 Acceptance   
  criteria\n 347 - scripts/check-protocol-drift.sh green (CI gate).\n 348 -     
  All built-in widgets round-trip a sample spec/action without data loss.\n     
  349 - Custom-widget extension point covered by a "hello world" test (e.g.,    
  openteam registers a SprintProgressWidget).\n 350 - Version-negotiation:      
  server emits version: 2, client only knows 1 → falls back gracefully + emits  
  telemetry event.\n 351 \n 352 Risks\n 353 - 🔴 Schema design errors           
  propagate to every consumer; backward-incompat changes are painful.           
  Mitigation: explicit version per widget kind +                                
  WidgetRegistry.adapt(fromVersion, toVersion) hook; SemVer-major bump          
  triggers RFC review.\n 354 - 🔴 Drift between Python & TS contracts → broken  
  renders in prod. Mitigation: single JSON Schema source + CI drift gate +      
  integration fixtures.\n 355 - 🟡 Python typing skew (TypedDict vs pydantic    
  vs dataclass). Mitigation: pydantic v2 canonical; provide a TypedDict export  
  for type-only consumers.\n 356 - 🟡 Dev-mode JSON Schema validation may slow  
  rendering. Mitigation: gate on NODE_ENV !== \'production\'.\n 357 \n 358      
  Validation: contract tests (pytest + vitest) cross-validate ≥ 20 spec         
  fixtures both ways; aggregated to widgets/contract/report.json.\n 359 \n 360  
  Rollback: keep version: 1 only; do not require consumers to upgrade; legacy   
  in-tree WidgetRegistry from openteam available behind                         
  widgets/src/chat-widgets/legacy/ re-export for one minor version.\n 361 \n    
  362 ### Phase 4 — Layout (≈ 3–5 days)\n 363 Scope: promote layout-shell       
  components, router-agnostic (slots for content).\n 364 \n 365 Deliverables:   
  widgets/src/layout/* — AppShell/AppHeader, Sidebar, TopBar, Splitter,         
  SettingsDrawer, ConnectionStatusBar, FileViewer, FolderTree. Responsive       
