  WidgetMessage.to_dict() byte-for-byte):\n 243 \n 244 json\n 245 {             
  "widget_id": "...", "widget_type": "single_choice",\n 246   "title": "...",   
  "description": "...",\n 247   "input_mode": { "mode": "...", "prompt":        
  "...", "options": [...] },\n 248   "fields": [ { "name": "...",               
  "widget_type": "...", ... } ],\n 249   "metadata": { ... } }\n 250 \n 251 \n  
  252 Canonical string constants (from widget_protocol.py): text_input,         
  single_choice, multiple_choice, dropdown, toggle, tool_argument_form.         
  Documented aliases (to be deprecated on a known timeline):                    
  free_text→text_input, multiple_choices→multiple_choice,                       
  press_to_continue→confirmation. Add WIDGET_CONFIRMATION = "confirmation" to   
  widget_protocol.py to close the Python-side gap.\n 253 \n 254 D2. Response    
  envelope. WidgetResponse.to_dict() shape: {widget_id, values, action ∈        
  {submit|cancel|skip}}. React onSubmit(result) MUST emit a                     
  WidgetResponse-shaped object; current ad-hoc shapes ({choice_index},          
  {custom_text}) are forbidden in canonical components.\n 255 \n 256 D3. React  
  <WidgetHost> contract. A small wrapper component that, given a WidgetMessage  
  JSON, calls registry.get(widget_type) and renders it; on submit invokes       
  onResponse(WidgetResponse). Each widget React component MUST accept props {   
  data, onSubmit(result), onCancel?, theme } where data is the deserialised     
  WidgetMessage. Falls back to DefaultWidget/UnknownWidget (named               
  DefaultWidget in canonical) — mirror of OT/RE pattern.\n 257 \n 258 D4.       
  Theme contract. Each widget reads optional                                    
  theme.custom.surfaces.{cardBorder, overlayLight, sidebarBg} slots already     
  used by OT FileViewer and ChatWidgetRenderer. Provide a fallback when those   
  slots are absent so widgets remain usable in an un-augmented MUI theme.\n     
