  \n  84 ---\n  85 \n  86 ## 1. High-Level Approach\n  87 \n  88 ### 1.1        
  Strategy\n  89 \n  90 1. OT as canonical stack target. OT is the newest       
  stack (React 19 / MUI 7) and the only one carrying first-class concepts like  
  theme.custom.* slots, WidgetRegistry driven by inputMode strings,             
  ThinkingFold / PromptViewerDrawer / FolderTree, and slash-command             
  autocomplete bound to useTaskTopologies. It is also the only one missing      
  WelcomeScreen — a regression to backfill from RE/AF.\n  91 2. RE react/src/   
  as the legacy reference. Richest widget registry (proposal_selection,         
  grouped, multi_input), proven axios transport, already migrated past the      
  react-markdown@9 inline removal. RE's legacy src/ sibling tree is dead        
  weight.\n  92 3. AF-proto as the canonical wire contract. widget_protocol.py  
  + input_modes.py already define InputMode, InputModeConfig, ChoiceOption,     
  WidgetMessage, WidgetField, WidgetResponse with to_dict()/from_dict(). Both   
  React registries already partly accept these strings. Unify React onto the    
  Python envelope.\n  93 4. AF-dash: concept-only parity. The Dash stack        
  cannot directly reuse React components, but the concepts (chat_window,        
  chat_history, file_viewer, log_graph, tabbed_panel) get a 1:1 conceptual map  
  in the matrix so a future migration is mechanical.\n  94 5. Two-artifact      
  deliverable. A workspace-level overlap_matrix.md (single index) plus one      
  canonical_contract/0N-*.md per cluster (per-concept design specs).            
  Cross-linked by anchor.\n  95 \n  96 ### 1.2 Architectural Decisions\n  97    
  \n  98 | Decision | Rationale (evidence) |\n  99 |---|---|\n 100 | Canonical  
  React stack = React 19 + MUI 7 (OT baseline) | OT is already there;           
  RE/AF-web upgrade is smaller-surface than downgrading OT. MUI 7 ships a       
  stable styled API; theme.custom.* augmentation is preserved. |\n 101 |        
  Canonical widget wire format = AF-proto (WidgetMessage / WidgetField /        
  WidgetResponse) | Already a serialised, server-authored contract with stable  
  string constants and to_dict()/from_dict(). Both React registries already     
  key on the same strings. |\n 102 | Single canonical React WidgetRegistry =    
  RE's superset + per-widget feature flag | OT registry (5 widgets,             
  slash-command-flavoured) ⊂ AF-web (10 widgets) ⊂ RE (11–13 widgets).          
  Superset avoids forking; registerWidgets({...}) opt-in keeps each app slim.   
  |\n 103 | ChatWidgetRenderer and WidgetRegistry separated by responsibility   
  | OT already does this split (Renderer = layout + dispatch; Registry =        
  lookup). Adopt OT's split everywhere. |\n 104 | Backfill WelcomeScreen from   
  RE/AF into OT verbatim | RE/AF WelcomeScreen.js is byte-identical (empty      
  diff -q); OT has no equivalent. |\n 105 | Mark legacy src/ trees in AF-web    
  and RE as deprecated (do not delete in this task) | RE                        
  src/components/widgets/ and AF-web src/components/widgets/ are empty stubs;   
  live trees are react/src/. Drift hazard — but deletion needs cross-repo       
  consumer scan first. |\n 106 | Document AF-dash parity only | Different       
  runtime (server-rendered Python). Track concept overlap in matrix only; no    
  code unification. |\n 107 | Cluster naming = "Concept" not "ComponentName" |  
  E.g. the markdownRenderer cluster covers renderer + CodeComponent sub-API.    
  Avoids naming bias. |\n 108 | Canonical pivot per cluster = strictest         
  implementation, with additive features behind slots | LoadingIndicator        
  canonical = byte-identical impl; MarkdownRenderer canonical = union API via   
  slots (renderCode, renderToolsToInvoke); WidgetRegistry canonical = RE        
  13-key superset; StreamingMessage canonical = OT phase machine (others        
  degrade trivially). |\n 109 | Theme contract = single token namespace         
