  Schema bridges widget_protocol.py and the React                               
  WidgetRegistry/ChatWidgetRenderer. Python is the source of truth — it emits   
  the JSON Schema, from which TS types are generated; a CI drift gate enforces  
  parity.\n  35 5. Staged migration ordered by dependency: bootstrap →          
  theme/primitives/hooks → chat primitives → chat-widgets+registry → layout →   
  consumer adoption → cleanup. Each phase ships independently and is            
  independently revertable.\n  36 \n  37 ### 1.2 Design Pillars\n  38 -         
  Backward compatibility first: each phase is shippable independently;          
  consumers opt-in per-component to avoid big-bang upgrades.\n  39 -            
  Peer-deps, not bundled deps: React, MUI, Emotion are peer deps so consumers   
  control versioning and bundle size (avoids "two Reacts" hooks errors).\n  40  
  - Theme as a contract, not a default: the library never imports a global      
  theme. Consumers wire their ThemeProvider; components read tokens via MUI's   
  useTheme() keyed against the documented token schema.\n  41 - Headless where  
  possible: chat-widgets accept a spec prop (matching the Python protocol) and  
  an onAction callback; rendering is local, transport is the consumer's         
  concern.\n  42 \n  43 ### 1.3 Non-goals (Phases 0–6)\n  44 - Rewriting        
