  197 #### Generalization of existing pieces\n 198 - `createAppTheme(tokens:    
  ThemeTokens, overrides?: DeepPartial) → MuiTheme` — generalization of         
  rankevolve's `createAppTheme(name, mode)` which hard-codes palettes. Tokens   
  first, MUI overrides second.\n 199 - `themeRegistry` — `Map<string,           
  ThemeTokens>` runtime singleton scoped per-consumer (avoids React-version     
  module duplication). Ships with three defaults (`light`, `dark`,              
  `highContrast`); consumers register additional themes.\n 200 -                
  `ThemeProvider` — wraps MUI `ThemeProvider` + emotion `CacheProvider` +       
  `CssBaseline`, and exposes raw tokens via a React context so non-MUI          
  components can read them.\n 201 - `ThemeSwitcher` — headless hook             
  (`useThemeSwitcher()`) + an opinionated MUI menu built on top;                
  uncontrolled+controlled prop pattern; `onChange(themeName)`.\n 202 -          
  `cssVariableBridge` — produces `--af-color-…`, `--af-spacing-…` CSS custom    
  properties so the Dash surface (and any non-React island) can read the same   
  tokens. This enables the dual-surface vision in §1.\n 203 \n 204 ####         
  Back-compat shims\n 205 - `widgets/src/theme/legacy/` exports rankevolve's    
  old names (`createAppTheme(name, mode)`) wrapping the new API for one minor   
  version, then removed in Phase 6.\n 206 \n 207 ### 2.4 Unified Widget         
  Contract (Decision D)\n 208 \n 209 Shared schema name: `WidgetSpec`. Python   
  is the source of truth (`widget_protocol.py`); a generator emits JSON         
  Schema; TS bindings are generated from the JSON Schema.\n 210 \n 211 text\n   
  212 WidgetSpec = {\n 213   id:          string                # stable        
  client id\n 214   kind:        string                # discriminator:         
  "approval" | "choice" | "confirmation" |\n 215                                
  #   "multiple_choice" | "single_choice" | "text_input" |\n 216                
  #   "conversation_tool" | "markdown" | "image" |\n 217                        
  #   "table" | "plot" | <custom>\n 218   version:     int                   #  
  integer major; minor changes are additive (OQ-12)\n 219   title?:             
  string\n 220   description?:string\n 221   payload:     Record<string, any>   
  # widget-kind-specific (schema-validated)\n 222   actions?:    Array<{ id;    
  label; style?; payload?: any }>\n 223   state?:      "pending" | "submitted"  
  | "expired" | "error"\n 224   created_at:  string                #            
  ISO-8601\n 225   metadata?:   Record<string, any>   # tracing, agent ids,     
  timestamps\n 226 }\n 227 \n 228 WidgetAction = {\n 229   widgetId:            
  string\n 230   actionId:    string\n 231   values?:     Record<string, any>   
  # form-style returns from input widgets\n 232   timestamp:   string           
  # ISO-8601\n 233 }\n 234 \n 235 \n 236 #### Python side (source of truth)\n   
  237 - `widget_protocol.py` (extended, backward-compatible):\n 238   -         
  Discriminated-union envelopes on `kind` using `pydantic.BaseModel`.\n 239     
