  `FormWidget`, `PlotWidget`, `ApprovalWidget`, `ConfirmationWidget`,           
  `MultipleChoiceWidget`, `SingleChoiceWidget`, `TextInputWidget`,              
  `ConversationToolWidget`, `CustomWidget`).\n 241   - Methods: `to_spec() ->   
  WidgetSpec`, `from_action(action: WidgetAction)`, `serialize_for_react()`     
  returns a JSON-serializable envelope consumable over any transport            
  (websocket, SSE, postMessage from a Dash iframe).\n 242   - Exposes           
  `WIDGET_SCHEMA` (the JSON Schema produced by `pydantic`).\n 243 -             
  `widget_schema.py` (new):\n 244   python\n 245   def emit_schema(path:        
  pathlib.Path) -> None: ...\n 246   # Invoked via Makefile target /            
  pre-commit hook; writes\n 247   #                                             
  agent_foundation/ui/widgets/schemas/widget-spec.schema.json\n 248   \n 249    
  \n 250 #### TypeScript side\n 251 - `scripts/generate-protocol.ts` runs       
  `json-schema-to-typescript` against `widget-spec.schema.json` → emits         
  `src/protocol/widget.generated.ts` (header: `// GENERATED — do not edit`).\n  
  252 - `chat-widgets/WidgetRegistry.ts`:\n 253   ts\n 254   type WidgetKind =  
  WidgetSpec[\'kind\'];\n 255   interface WidgetRenderer<K extends WidgetKind>  
  {\n 256     kind: K; version: number;\n 257     component:                    
  React.ComponentType<{ spec: Extract<WidgetSpec, {kind: K}>; onAction: (a:     
  WidgetAction) => void; }>;\n 258   }\n 259   class WidgetRegistry {           
  register(...); get(kind, version); render(spec, onAction);                    
  adapt(fromVersion, toVersion) }\n 260   \n 261   The registry is              
  transport-agnostic and version-aware (per-widget `version` + `adapt()`        
  migration hook for forward-compat).\n 262 -                                   
  `chat-widgets/ChatWidgetRenderer.tsx`: thin component ``. Validates spec      
  against JSON Schema in dev-mode only (opt-out in prod). Provides `` when      
