  headless+typed: this is the only design that satisfies both surfaces (Dash    
  sends JSON; React consumes JSON) without coupling either to the other's       
  framework.\n 273 \n 274 ---\n 275 \n 276 ## 3. Phased Migration Plan\n 277    
  \n 278 Each phase has: scope, deliverables, acceptance criteria, risks,       
  validation, rollback. Phases are sequential; within a phase, sub-items can    
  parallelize. "Done" = acceptance criteria all green + at least one consumer   
  integration test green where applicable.\n 279 \n 280 ### Phase 0 —           
  Bootstrap (≈ 2–3 days, no consumer changes)\n 281 Scope: scaffold             
  `agent_foundation/ui/widgets/` (package.json, tsconfig, tsup, vitest, lint,   
  CI matrix on {React 18, React 19} × {MUI 5, MUI 7} = 4 cells (the `(React 18  
  + MUI 7)` and `(React 19 + MUI 5)` cells run as non-blocking smoke            
  compatibility jobs; the `(React 18 + MUI 5)` and `(React 19 + MUI 7)` cells   
  are blocking and gate merges), Storybook). Add `webui/README.md` DEPRECATED   
  notice. Inventory out-of-tree consumers of vendored `webui` (R-07).\n 282 \n  
  283 Deliverables: empty package builds & publishes a `0.0.0` smoke artifact;  
  CI green; Storybook hosting decided (OQ-8).\n 284 \n 285 Risks: 🟢 Tooling    
  churn.\n 286 \n 287 Validation: `pnpm -F @agent-foundation/ui-widgets build   
  && pnpm -F @agent-foundation/ui-widgets test && npm pack` succeed in CI.\n    
  288 \n 289 Rollback: delete `widgets/` directory; no consumer touched.\n 290  
  \n 291 ### Phase 1 — Theme + Primitives + Hooks (Foundation, ≈ 1 week)\n 292  
  Scope: port primitives (LoadingIndicator, EmptyState, SectionCard,            
  StatusBadge, PersonChip, ProgressBar, QuickLinkButton, PendingReasonPopover,  
  MarkdownRenderer, Button, Card, Stack, Icon, Tooltip), `theme/`, generic      
  `hooks/` from rankevolve & openteam, reconciling APIs to the token schema.\n  
  293 \n 294 Deliverables\n 295 - `widgets/src/{primitives,theme,hooks}/` with  
  Storybook stories per export.\n 296 -                                         
  `widgets/src/theme/{tokens,createAppTheme,themeRegistry,ThemeProvider,ThemeS  
  witcher,cssVariableBridge,legacy}/`.\n 297 - CI: lint + typecheck + unit      
  tests + storybook build.\n 298 \n 299 Acceptance criteria\n 300 - `pnpm -F    
  @agent-foundation/ui-widgets build` produces ESM + CJS + .d.ts.\n 301 - A     
  scratch app on React 18 + MUI 5 renders every primitive without errors        
  (blocking gate — matches the declared peer-dep floor).\n 302 - A scratch app  
  on React 19 + MUI 7 renders every primitive without errors (non-blocking      
  smoke compatibility check; aligns with the openteam consumer profile and the  
  Phase 0 CI matrix's React 19 cells).\n 303 - `createAppTheme(lightTokens)`    
  survives both MUI v5 and v7 type checks.\n 304 - Theme tokens snapshot test   
  passes; 100% of exports have Storybook story + TSDoc.\n 305 \n 306 Risks\n    
  307 - 🟡 `MarkdownRenderer` has three subtly-different versions across        
  codebases. Mitigation: pick rankevolve's (smallest deps) as canonical, file   
  diffs as backlog.\n 308 - 🟡 Subtle MUI v5↔v7 API drift inside primitives.    
  Mitigation: CI matrix against both; encapsulate MUI calls inside              
  primitives.\n 309 - 🟢 Bundle size growth — mitigated by sub-path exports +   
  `size-limit` (<25 kB gz for primitives).\n 310 \n 311 Validation:             
  jest/vitest + RTL unit tests; visual regression baseline via                  
  `@storybook/test-runner`; type-coverage ≥ 95%.\n 312 \n 313 Rollback:         
  package unimported by any consumer; rollback = delete `widgets/`              
  directory.\n 314 \n 315 ### Phase 2 — Chat Primitives (≈ 1 week)\n 316        
  Scope: promote chat-leaf components, headless w.r.t. transport (no fetch, no  
  websocket).\n 317 \n 318 Deliverables: `widgets/src/chat/` — MessageList,     
  MessageBubble, Composer/ChatInput, CommandAutocomplete, StreamingMessage,     
  AgentMessageBubble, ThinkingFold, Breadcrumb, NodeDetailPanel,                
  PromptViewerDrawer, SessionContextBar. Each ships with Storybook + tests +    
